<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan construction orders fall 6.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan construction orders fall 6.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's construction orders fell 6.3 percent in January from a year earlier to 1.22 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of January construction orders (in billions of yen unless specified, with year-on-year changes):</p>
<p> Domestic private-sector orders		 737,398   +9.7</p>
<p> Domestic public-sector orders		  342,639  -33.8</p>
<p>Foreign government facilities in Japan and</p>
<p> orders of less than 10 million yen	    32,548   -3.9</p>
<p> Orders received abroad			   108,593  +36.3</p>
<p> Total						 1.22 trln  -6.3</p>
</text>
